[system]
You are an academic paper structure classifier. Your job is to identify which sections are needed to write a one-sentence TLDR of the paper.

[user]
The following section headers were found in an academic paper:
{sections}

Return ONLY a JSON object with one key:
{{"key_sections": ["<header1>", "<header2>", ...]}}

Keep only the sections that directly state what the paper is about and what it achieves:
- Always include: Abstract, Introduction, Conclusion (and variants like "Discussion", "Summary", "Closing Remarks")
- Include if present: a section naming the proposed method/system, and a high-level results or contributions section
- Omit: detailed methodology, mathematical derivations, implementation details, related work, experiments setup, ablations, appendices, acknowledgements, references

Copy header strings exactly as they appear above — no paraphrasing.
Aim for 2–4 sections. If the paper has no abstract or conclusion, include the next best substitute.
